# No Cursor Attribution

In this repository, **never** add any Cursor-related attribution to:

- **Commit messages** — do not append `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` or any similar trailer
- **Pull request titles or descriptions** — no "Made with Cursor", "Generated by Cursor", emoji-prefixed AI badges, or co-author callouts
- **Code comments** — no `// Generated by Cursor` / `# Made with Cursor` / etc.
- **Documentation, READMEs, changelogs**

When invoking `git commit`, pass the message via `-m` or HEREDOC exactly as you intended it; do not let any agent integration append a trailer. If you find yourself about to add a co-author line, stop.

A local `commit-msg` git hook in `.git/hooks/commit-msg` enforces this automatically as defense-in-depth. Do not modify or remove that hook.

## Why

This is a personal portfolio repo. The owner wants the git history to reflect only their own authorship without IDE branding baked into the project record.
